---
// src/components/SideRail.astro — the case-study side rail.
//
// The frame only. What goes in it is passed as named slots, each expected to
// be a .rail-section (see Contents / RailAction) — the rule between sections
// is drawn by the section itself off a sibling selector, so adding or dropping
// one never leaves a hanging line. Styling lives in pages/projects/[id].astro
// with the rest of the case-study rules.
//
// The back link is not a slot because it is not optional: it is the way out of
// the page.
interface Props {
  backHref?: string;
  backLabel?: string;
}
const { backHref = "/", backLabel = "All work" } = Astro.props;
---
<aside class="rail">
  <!-- Everything in here carries [data-snap], written by hand in each
       component, and deliberately NOT [data-snap-all]: the layout's tagger
       snaps every `li` it finds, but in the contents list the <li> is a
       wrapper around a grid <a> that is the real row. Snapping both nests two
       baseline transforms and the first entry lands on the label's line.

       The snap is measured in page space, so the rail is exact at rest. Once
       `position: sticky` pins it, it rides the viewport and the block floats
       against the painted lines behind it. That is the accepted trade — the
       alternative, recomputing `top` per frame to hold the rail congruent to
       the grid, is a sawtooth: the rail scrolls with the page for 32px then
       jumps 32px to catch up, stuttering the whole left side of the page once
       per row while you read.

       [data-snap-sticky] is what makes the first half of that paragraph true.
       Without it "measured in page space" was aspirational: a pinned element
       reports where it is PAINTED, so any pass that ran while the page was
       scrolled snapped the rail against the viewport instead, and rows that
       rounded opposite ways ended up a whole span apart. The snapper switches
       this element to `position: static` for the length of its measurements —
       see the note over `pinned` in BaseLayout. -->
  <div class="rail-inner" data-snap-sticky>
    <a class="rail-back" href={backHref} data-snap>&larr; {backLabel}</a>
    <slot name="contents" />
    <slot name="action" />
  </div>
</aside>
